Reconciliation is the process React uses to:

compare old UI with new UI

and update only the changed parts.

Simple Example

Suppose your screen shows:

<h1>Count: 0</h1>

Now user clicks button.

State changes:

setCount(1)

Now React creates new UI:

<h1>Count: 1</h1>

React now compares:

OLD:

<h1>Count: 0</h1>

NEW:

<h1>Count: 1</h1>

It notices:

Only text changed

So React updates only that text.

This comparison process is called:

Reconciliation


